# Provider model options (extendParams / option menus)

Custom “model extension” toggles (gear icon → popover) **must stay aligned with what each vendor’s HTTP API actually accepts.** Wrong or invented parameters cause empty responses, rejected requests, or broken tool calling.

## Authority order

1. **Official vendor documentation** — API reference, OpenAPI/schema, changelog, model tables (“only model `X` accepts field `Y`”).
2. **Structured schema** — e.g. Moonshot chat request `components/schemas/KimiK26ChatRequest` on [platform.moonshot.cn docs](https://platform.moonshot.cn/docs/api/chat).
3. **Secondary research** — Context7 / MCP docs fetch **only when** grounded in vendor docs; resolve conflicts in favor of the vendor.

Do **not** expose a toggle because another provider has a similarly named feature. Do **not** invent request-body keys (e.g. Minimax/OpenAI-compat flags) without documentation.

## End-to-end mapping (every new option)

Each real capability should be traced through **all** of these unless intentionally UI-only:

| Layer | Location (typical) |
|-------|-------------------|
| Catalogue | `packages/model-bank/src/aiModels/<provider>.ts` — `settings.extendParams?: ExtendParamsType[]` per **model id** |
| ExtendParams union | `packages/model-bank/src/types/aiModel.ts` — add a new union member only when wiring is real |
| Agent config | `packages/types/src/agent/chatConfig.ts` — field + `AgentChatConfigSchema` when persisted |
| Request assembly | `src/services/chat/index.ts` — map `chatConfig` → `ChatStreamPayload` / `extendParams` |
| Provider runtime | `packages/model-runtime/src/providers/<provider>/` — exact JSON body; unit tests for payload shape |
| UI | Provider-specific panel (see below) + i18n (`src/locales/default/chat.ts` + `locales/en-US|zh-CN/chat.json`) |

If the doc says a field applies **only** to certain model IDs, gate **`extendParams` on those cards** and gate runtime branches on `payload.model` — do not send the field for other ids.

## Fetched model list normalization

When a provider supports **Fetch models**, the fetched API list must be normalized to the same capability model as the built-in model bank:

- Use `processModelList(..., MODEL_LIST_CONFIGS.<provider>, ModelProvider.<Provider>)` or an equivalent provider-specific normalizer in `packages/model-runtime/src/providers/<provider>/`.
- Add provider keywords in `packages/model-runtime/src/utils/modelParse.ts` for newly released ids so fetched models get `functionCall`, `reasoning`, `vision`, `video`, `search`, and `imageOutput` consistently.
- If the remote model table cannot store `settings.extendParams`, add a **read-time only** settings inference in `packages/database/src/repositories/aiInfra/index.ts` for the exact provider/model family. Do not persist inferred `settings` into the remote model record.
- Keep inference provider-scoped. For example, DeepSeek V4 can infer `['enableReasoning', 'reasoningEffort']`, MiniMax M-series can infer `['minimaxReasoningSplit']`, Moonshot K2.5/K2.6 can infer their documented toggles, but Kimi K2.7 Code must not expose a toggle because thinking/preserved reasoning is forced by the provider.

## Provider context and stripped request fields

When stripping request-body fields such as legacy generic sampling params or user-supplied `provider`, preserve the trusted server-side provider context from routing/runtime initialization. Runtime converters, tracing, and stream error handling may still need `payload.provider` internally (for example OpenAI-compatible usage accounting for `xai` and `moonshot`), but that value must come from the trusted route/provider selection, not the serialized client body.

## Compatible provider guardrails

`openaicompatible` and `anthropiccompatible` are compatibility shims for known built-in model cards, not arbitrary capability clones of OpenAI/Anthropic:

- Keep their model lists fixed to model-bank IDs sourced from the native provider lists; do not re-enable arbitrary add/fetch UI without a separate design.
- Native model search is **opt-in**: model cards keep `abilities.search: false` (no auto-tag) but retain `settings.searchImpl: 'params'` so the "Use the model's built-in search engine" toggle appears in the search panel. When the toggle is OFF (default), ChatHub uses its own web-browsing tools; when ON, `enabledSearch` is carried in the internal payload for runtime/tool handling, and provider adapters must only send upstream search fields documented by that provider.
- OpenAI-compatible Responses API mode is opt-in only. Default to Chat Completions mode; enable Responses API only when the gateway documents `/v1/responses`, typed event streaming, and compatible tool/search behavior.
- OpenAI-compatible request conversion, terminal events, callback success rules, cancellation, tool correlation, usage accounting, and diagnostic redaction are defined in `.cursor/rules/openai-compatible-runtime.mdc`.
- GPT-5 reasoning effort is **model-specific** and must use `resolveGPT5ReasoningEffort` from `@lobechat/types` in both UI and request assembly. Although OpenAI accepts lower reasoning efforts, ChatHub intentionally applies a quality floor: `gpt-5.6-sol` exposes `high`, `xhigh`, `max`, while GPT-5.5 exposes `high`, `xhigh`. Lower, unset, or otherwise unsupported saved values for those families resolve to `high`; persisted legacy values remain schema-valid. Earlier GPT-5 models keep `minimal` through `high` and fall back to `medium`. Chat Completions sends top-level `reasoning_effort`; Responses maps it to `reasoning.effort`.
- OpenAI-compatible cache behavior is a provider-settings matrix, not a model gear option. Preserve `openAICompatCache` and `openAICompatResponsesParams` end to end: visible presets are `prompt-key-store` and `custom`, legacy saved presets `pptoken.org` and `apikl.ai` normalize to `prompt-key-store`, and runtime strips internal cache fields before upstream requests. Detailed cache matrix, debugging, and provider-probe guidance lives in `.cursor/rules/prompt-cache-stability.mdc`.
- Anthropic-compatible calls target Anthropic Messages semantics; expose Anthropic-only toggles only when the compatibility endpoint documents the same accepted request fields.

## UI pattern: one provider panel at a time

- **Dispatcher:** `src/features/ChatInput/ActionBar/Model/index.tsx` — route by runtime **provider id**:

  | Provider id | Component |
  | ----------- | --------- |
  | `moonshot` | `providers/MoonshotOptions.tsx` |
  | `minimax` | `providers/MinimaxOptions.tsx` |
  | `anthropic` | `providers/AnthropicOptions.tsx` |
  | `openai` | `providers/OpenAIOptions.tsx` |
  | *everything else* | `ControlsForm.tsx` |

- **Provider component:** under `.../Model/providers/<Name>Options.tsx` — build **only** fields implied by `aiModelSelectors.modelExtendParams(model, provider)`. Use **compact** popovers (`minWidth` ~320px for dedicated panels), vertical slider rows when needed, optional **scroll** (`maxHeight`) — avoid Claude-only copy on non-Anthropic panels.
- **Migration strategy:** ship **one** new provider panel per focused change; keep `ControlsForm` for unmigrated providers.

Gear visibility remains **`isModelHasExtendParams`** — empty `extendParams` means no gear.

## Chat request shaping (MiniMax)

When **MiniMax** rejects requests with context overflow (**`bad_request_error` / 2013**), the fork trims chat history in **`src/services/chat/trimMinimaxContext.ts`** (called from **`src/services/chat/index.ts`**) so **`messages` + `tools`** fit the **effective** input budget. Coordinate with gear / tool UX if payload size changes.

## Testing and regression

- Add or extend **runtime unit tests** on `build*Payload` / `handlePayload` when behavior is non-trivial (thinking toggles, tool + thinking interaction, optional fields like `thinking.keep`).
- For OpenAI-compatible cache changes, test both `/v1/chat/completions` and `/v1/responses` body/header shapes, including `Session_id`-only Responses mode and legacy `responseStateMode` normalization.
- After changes, run **`bash scripts/type-check-tsc.sh`** and targeted Vitest commands from `.cursor/rules/commands.mdc` (for example, **`bunx vitest run --silent='passed-only' '<file>'`**) for touched packages.
- For model option-panel changes, do not start a local dev server or browser-level visual check unless the user explicitly requests it. Complete unit and type-check verification locally, then verify the rendered panel after the canary build completes and the image is available.

## Shipping

Follow **`.cursor/rules/git-and-release.mdc`** — **no commit / tag / push without an explicit in-turn user instruction** unless the user asked to ship.

## Quick checklist (new module or new toggle)

- [ ] Confirmed in **official** API docs / schema for **this** model id.
- [ ] `extendParams` updated on the right model card(s); union type extended if new key.
- [ ] `chatConfig` + Zod if persisted; service mapping updated.
- [ ] Provider runtime sends **only** documented fields; tests updated.
- [ ] Provider option panel + i18n; no shared Anthropic-specific copy on other vendors.
